{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>כי אם</b>. If a man knew that he would live many years and rejoice in all of them — when he remembers the days of darkness, which are the days of the grave, for they will be many, the mentioned light will be bitter to him. And all that comes — its matter is vanity, for he will understand that all that comes to all of them, a generation goes and a generation comes, is vanity."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The reading 'ימר' appears to be a form of ימיר (will change/exchange); the sense is that the remembered light turns bitter by contrast. Alternatively possibly corrupt for ימרר (will embitter). The clause 'וכל שבא הבל ענינו יבין' is textually strained; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:10.830117852Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}